# The installer's kernel (G1.6c, os/package/corerouter-installer): the
# image's final .config with these on top. The command line has no root=:
# the kernel runs /init from the embedded initramfs (corerouter-init,
# which sees corerouter.mode=live: G1.6y, it moves to the image's root read
# from the medium, or stays on the console installer when it cannot). No
# BTF: nothing here needs eBPF yet (XDP is off in the live image), and
# kbuild then has no pahole step (faster relink, smaller kernel).
CONFIG_CMDLINE_BOOL=y
CONFIG_CMDLINE="console=tty0 console=ttyS0,115200 corerouter.mode=live panic=10 quiet"
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y
CONFIG_RD_ZSTD=y
CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_ZSTD=y
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_DWARF_TOOLCHAIN_DEFAULT is not set
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_NONE=y
# G1.6j: the installer and the live image load no modules (the ones in the
# image were built for the installed kernel), so a card must be built in here
# to show a port on the ISO. The E810 runs in Safe Mode without its firmware
# (it asks while probing, before the root is there), enough to show the port;
# it works in full on the installed router. The others ask at open, or need
# nothing. These are the common cards; the rest of nics.fragment gets its port
# on the installed router only (docs/os-image.md has the table).
CONFIG_ICE=y
CONFIG_BNXT=y
CONFIG_BNX2=y
CONFIG_BNX2X=y
CONFIG_MLX4_EN=y
CONFIG_SFC=y
CONFIG_AQTION=y
CONFIG_ALX=y
CONFIG_ATL1C=y
CONFIG_SKY2=y
CONFIG_8139TOO=y
